{"name":"Create faceless video voice-overs in batch with Gemini TTS, script checks, listen-back QA and Telegram approval","nodes":[{"id":"a6536d9e-5594-439f-a477-ca618669bbaa","name":"Sticky Note","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[-870,-88],"parameters":{"width":560,"height":966,"content":"## Faceless voice-overs in batch with Gemini TTS\n\n**For** faceless channels (YouTube, TikTok, Reels) that publish many narrated videos.\n\n### How it works\n1. Add topics with the **Add Topics Form** (saved in the `vs_queue` Data Table).\n2. Every morning **Gemini** writes a script per topic, directed by its niche and format (Short, explainer or story).\n3. **Script checks**: length, hook, scenes, filler phrases and a list of facts to verify. One automatic fix if needed.\n4. **Gemini TTS** voices it (a backup model steps in if the first fails). Scenes are timed to the real pauses and an SRT is built.\n5. **Listen-back check**: Gemini transcribes the audio and compares it with the script.\n6. **Telegram** brings you the audio and the script file (scene times, facts to verify, a Suno Speech block): ✅ use it or 🔁 redo.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. **Google Gemini (PaLM) API** credential (free key at aistudio.google.com): select it in the 4 Gemini nodes and in the 2 **Generate Voice** nodes.\n2. **Telegram API** credential (token from @BotFather): select it in the 6 Telegram nodes, then send /start to your bot.\n3. **Set Channel Settings**: channel name, your angle, `telegram_chat_id` (from @userinfobot) and `batch_size`.\n4. Click ▶ next to **Run Every Morning** to run the pinned example topic. Then unpin **Get Next Queued Topics**, add topics with the form and publish.\n\n### Requirements\n- n8n with Data Tables (Cloud or recent self-hosted; built on 2.41.6), reachable over public HTTPS for the approval buttons.\n- A Gemini API key (the free tier is enough to start) and a Telegram bot.\n\n### Customization\nNiches, voices and formats live in **Build Voice Direction Prompt**; the run time in **Run Every Morning**. Set `listen_back_check` to false to skip the transcription.\n\nMade by **Amelqa** · amelqa.com"},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"d5606b31-e6d0-4985-ae55-767c980b0bf0","name":"Sticky Note1","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[-190,-88],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":1360,"height":786,"content":"## 1 · Take the next topics\nEvery morning: the next `batch_size` topics with status `queued` from the `vs_queue` Data Table (created on the first run). One example topic is pinned for your first test."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"1fe47ef0-4298-4eda-aaee-ce6c90a5808f","name":"Sticky Note2","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[1200,371],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":794,"height":557,"content":"## 2 · Write the script\nNiche and format set the voice, the style, the structure and the length. A backup Gemini model takes over if the first one fails."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"8b793ee5-01fb-4c75-ad03-9fd456b5f877","name":"Sticky Note3","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[2080,392],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":1810,"height":306,"content":"## 3 · Check the script\nLength, hook, scene count, filler phrases, footage searches and facts to verify. If something fails, Gemini fixes it once and the better version wins."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"4e00365e-173b-40f6-acc7-51f42594be74","name":"Sticky Note4","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[3920,371],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":710,"height":557,"content":"## 4 · Voice it\nGemini 3.8 TTS reads the script word for word with the niche style. WAV out, no FFmpeg: scenes are timed to the real pauses and captions (SRT) are built."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"f24f5f7b-9622-4490-abae-13363d1fd06c","name":"Sticky Note5","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[4660,392],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":1170,"height":306,"content":"## 5 · Listen back\nGemini transcribes the audio and compares it with the script word by word. Skipped or invented words show up in the review."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"a1f78782-9290-4f5c-a673-fcd4408e5602","name":"Sticky Note6","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[5860,-78],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":290,"height":836,"content":"## 6 · Save and hand off\nStatus, checks, listen-back score, facts and the full package (scenes with times and SRT) go to the topic row. Then each voice-over starts its own review run."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"76b16119-b457-4fbe-ac87-dd917a8bb279","name":"Sticky Note7","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[6210,272],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":3280,"height":566,"content":"## 7 · Review on Telegram\nThis workflow calls itself once per voice-over, so each one waits for your answer on its own: audio, script file and two buttons. ✅ marks the row `approved`, 🔁 puts the topic back in the queue."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"9e00ea76-42be-4178-ad4c-d7ee477034b2","name":"Sticky Note8","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[1400,1092],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":1610,"height":306,"content":"## Never silent\nEmpty queue, or Gemini wrote no script? One Telegram message tells you, and those topics stay queued for the next run."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"b5690b6f-318e-4b79-a729-0c1b48d3e57d","name":"Sticky Note9","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[-190,1832],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":1360,"height":306,"content":"## Add topics\nOpen the form URL, write one topic per line and pick niche, format and language. Each topic becomes a `queued` row, one day apart."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"b943391b-5f1b-4a3d-bf4b-bfc51123a772","name":"Run Every Morning","type":"n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger","position":[0,480],"parameters":{"rule":{"interval":[{"field":"days","triggerAtHour":7}]}},"typeVersion":1.2},{"id":"6520ecdd-b232-418c-97a7-2f788105f82b","name":"Set Channel Settings","type":"n8n-nodes-base.set","position":[320,480],"parameters":{"options":{},"assignments":{"assignments":[{"id":"f8b953b0-a3d2-44f0-bb83-9c7998d7cfdd","name":"channel_name","type":"string","value":"Your channel name"},{"id":"f7c99956-3ce8-4d97-9927-fb5bcf065e52","name":"channel_angle","type":"string","value":"What makes your channel different, in one line"},{"id":"07edc64f-ce11-4a33-b655-04954aaee635","name":"telegram_chat_id","type":"string","value":""},{"id":"8fc772be-948a-43ea-b4a5-b312bd173972","name":"batch_size","type":"number","value":3},{"id":"d32f3160-dd02-4ee6-9896-be5f31dd0025","name":"default_language","type":"string","value":"en"},{"id":"1c3f2731-0926-487a-8d2d-47d90eb70535","name":"listen_back_check","type":"boolean","value":true},{"id":"eb36b20a-6e5b-488a-a5f0-a1bd7e30929d","name":"suno_music","type":"boolean","value":true},{"id":"1a33dd93-fe2f-4241-984c-90ddf380dcae","name":"tts_model","type":"string","value":"gemini-3.8-flash-tts"},{"id":"e28f023b-3a19-45ed-9b66-6888640576dc","name":"tts_backup_model","type":"string","value":"gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts"},{"id":"43b8fbbf-ebd5-4e19-99c2-01476181fe5a","name":"approver_user_id","type":"string","value":""},{"id":"c0dfd8bc-1370-45a9-aaf1-5b5054017af9","name":"wait_hours","type":"number","value":48}]},"includeOtherFields":true},"typeVersion":3.4},{"id":"2183f608-c2a1-4d12-89e1-b7dc32c6eee1","name":"Create Queue Table If Missing","type":"n8n-nodes-base.dataTable","position":[640,0],"parameters":{"columns":{"column":[{"name":"topic","type":"string"},{"name":"niche","type":"string"},{"name":"format","type":"string"},{"name":"language","type":"string"},{"name":"voice","type":"string"},{"name":"notes","type":"string"},{"name":"publish_date","type":"date"},{"name":"status","type":"string"},{"name":"title","type":"string"},{"name":"words","type":"number"},{"name":"duration_s","type":"number"},{"name":"engine","type":"string"},{"name":"checks","type":"string"},{"name":"listen_back","type":"number"},{"name":"facts_to_verify","type":"string"},{"name":"suno_prompt","type":"string"},{"name":"package_json","type":"string"},{"name":"audio_file_id","type":"string"},{"name":"updated","type":"date"}]},"options":{"createIfNotExists":true},"resource":"table","operation":"create","tableName":"vs_queue"},"executeOnce":true,"typeVersion":1},{"id":"29a7009e-d6cc-43d9-a8fd-2549774ca6a5","name":"Get Next Queued Topics","type":"n8n-nodes-base.dataTable","position":[640,480],"parameters":{"limit":"={{ $('Set Channel Settings').first().json.batch_size }}","filters":{"conditions":[{"keyName":"status","keyValue":"queued","condition":"eq"}]},"orderBy":true,"resource":"row","matchType":"allConditions","operation":"get","returnAll":false,"dataTableId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"name","value":"vs_queue"},"orderByColumn":"publish_date","orderByDirection":"ASC"},"typeVersion":1,"alwaysOutputData":true},{"id":"b229f21a-ab1d-42c4-9b88-34ed73505985","name":"Check Queue Has Topics","type":"n8n-nodes-base.if","position":[960,480],"parameters":{"options":{},"conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"1e6efce7-fb2a-4c72-889a-1f94bb55e765","operator":{"type":"string","operation":"notEmpty","singleValue":true},"leftValue":"={{ $json.topic }}","rightValue":""}]}},"typeVersion":2.2},{"id":"ac069e0a-50a8-4d28-9573-5bf424c13618","name":"Notify Empty Queue","type":"n8n-nodes-base.telegram","onError":"continueRegularOutput","position":[1480,1180],"parameters":{"text":"🎙️ Voice Studio: your queue is empty. Add topics with the “Add topics” form and the next run will voice them.","chatId":"={{ $('Set Channel Settings').first().json.telegram_chat_id }}","additionalFields":{"appendAttribution":false,"disable_web_page_preview":true}},"typeVersion":1.2},{"id":"0a167811-3f7e-44dd-999b-e6aa1f425509","name":"Build Voice Direction Prompt","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[1280,480],"parameters":{"mode":"runOnceForEachItem","jsCode":"const LIB = {\"formats\":{\"short\":{\"label\":\"Short · 45–60 s, vertical\",\"seconds\":[45,60],\"wpm\":160,\"scenes\":[4,7],\"hookMax\":14,\"pace\":\"brisk and punchy, short sentences, tiny pauses between beats\",\"beats\":[\"Hook (0–3 s): one surprising line, 14 words at most, no greeting\",\"Context (3–10 s): why it matters, one sentence\",\"Three beats: one fact or turn per scene\",\"Payoff: answer the promise of the hook in plain words\",\"Loop: a last line that sends the viewer back to the start or on to the next video\"]},\"explainer\":{\"label\":\"Explainer · 2–3 min\",\"seconds\":[120,180],\"wpm\":150,\"scenes\":[6,12],\"hookMax\":16,\"pace\":\"clear and steady, a breath between sections, emphasis on the key word of each sentence\",\"beats\":[\"Hook (0–5 s): a question or contradiction the video will answer\",\"Promise (5–15 s): what the viewer will understand by the end\",\"Setup: the minimum background, with one analogy\",\"Three or four steps or reasons, each with a concrete example\",\"Twist: the part most people get wrong\",\"Payoff: answer the opening question in one sentence\",\"Close: a one-line recap and the next question\"]},\"story\":{\"label\":\"Story · 4–6 min\",\"seconds\":[240,360],\"wpm\":145,\"scenes\":[10,18],\"hookMax\":16,\"pace\":\"measured, letting key lines land, longer pauses at each turn of the story\",\"beats\":[\"Cold open: drop into a moment of tension, no introduction\",\"Who and where: the person or place in two sentences\",\"Rising stakes: three turns, each one raises a new question\",\"Midpoint reveal: the fact that changes how we see it\",\"Climax: the decisive moment, slower\",\"Resolution: what happened next, with one concrete detail\",\"Reflection: why it still matters, from your angle\",\"Close: one line that lingers\"]}},\"niches\":{\"history\":{\"label\":\"History stories\",\"voice\":\"Charon\",\"alt\":\"Sulafat\",\"gender\":\"male\",\"style\":\"documentary narrator: warm, low and unhurried, quietly intrigued, landing names and dates clearly\",\"arc\":\"curious → tense → reflective\",\"suno\":{\"voice\":\"deep warm documentary narrator, unhurried, intimate\",\"music\":\"cinematic documentary underscore, low strings and soft piano, no drums, voice-forward mix\",\"variation\":\"low\"},\"hooks\":[\"In [year], [person] did [unexpected thing]. Nobody expected what came next.\",\"This [object] changed [something big], and almost nobody knows its name.\",\"Everyone remembers [famous event]. Few remember what happened the night before.\"],\"pronounce\":\"Write years the way they are said (“fifteen eighteen”), say “Louis the Fourteenth”, not “Louis XIV”, and list foreign names with a respelling.\",\"visuals\":\"maps, public-domain engravings and archive photos, slow pans\",\"avoid\":\"graphic violence, present-day politics, unverified quotes\"},\"science\":{\"label\":\"Science & how it works\",\"voice\":\"Sadaltager\",\"alt\":\"Erinome\",\"gender\":\"female\",\"style\":\"friendly science explainer: bright, clear and curious, a smile in the voice, leaning on the surprising word of each sentence\",\"arc\":\"puzzled → aha → delighted\",\"suno\":{\"voice\":\"bright, clear and friendly explainer voice, curious\",\"music\":\"light curious electronic underscore, soft plucks and pads, steady gentle pulse, low in the mix\",\"variation\":\"low\"},\"hooks\":[\"Why does [everyday thing] [do odd thing]? The answer is stranger than you think.\",\"If [X] were the size of [Y], [surprising consequence].\",\"[Common belief]? Not quite. Here is what is really happening.\"],\"pronounce\":\"Spell out units (“kilometres per second”), round big numbers and say them naturally (“about three hundred thousand”), read formulas in words.\",\"visuals\":\"diagrams, macro footage, simple animations\",\"avoid\":\"health or medical claims, miracle cures, diet advice\"},\"space\":{\"label\":\"Space & astronomy\",\"voice\":\"Algieba\",\"alt\":\"Despina\",\"gender\":\"male\",\"style\":\"calm narrator full of wonder: soft, spacious and slow, hushed on the big numbers, awe in the voice\",\"arc\":\"quiet → awe → humble\",\"suno\":{\"voice\":\"soft spacious narrator, hushed wonder, slow\",\"music\":\"ambient space pads, slow evolving synths, distant shimmer, no beat\",\"variation\":\"low\"},\"hooks\":[\"Right now, above your head, [something enormous] is happening.\",\"Light from [object] left it [time] ago. You are seeing the past.\",\"There is a place in our solar system where [strange fact].\"],\"pronounce\":\"Turn huge numbers into comparisons, say “light-years” in full, and respell names (Betelgeuse: BEE-tel-jooz).\",\"visuals\":\"telescope imagery, star fields, slow zooms\",\"avoid\":\"astrology, doomsday claims\"},\"tech\":{\"label\":\"Tech & AI explained\",\"voice\":\"Iapetus\",\"alt\":\"Kore\",\"gender\":\"male\",\"style\":\"sharp tech explainer: confident, crisp and modern, quick but never rushed, a small lift of energy on each takeaway\",\"arc\":\"intrigued → clear → empowered\",\"suno\":{\"voice\":\"crisp confident tech explainer, modern, clear\",\"music\":\"minimal modern electronic, clean synth pulse, light glitch textures, ducked under the voice\",\"variation\":\"low\"},\"hooks\":[\"Your phone does [hidden thing] every time you [action].\",\"[Technology] sounds complicated. It is three simple ideas.\",\"In [year], [thing] was science fiction. Today it [does what].\"],\"pronounce\":\"Decide letters or word for each acronym (“A-P-I”, but “NASA”), say versions as spoken (“two point five”) and respell product names when needed.\",\"visuals\":\"screen recordings, close-ups of devices, simple motion graphics\",\"avoid\":\"crypto, trading or investment tips, rumours presented as facts\"}},\"cliches\":[\"in this video\",\"in today's video\",\"let's dive in\",\"dive into\",\"buckle up\",\"without further ado\",\"smash that like\",\"you won't believe\",\"stay tuned\",\"hey guys\",\"welcome back\",\"let's get started\",\"mind-blowing\",\"game-changer\",\"delve\"],\"tags\":[\"<short pause>\",\"<long pause>\",\"<breath>\",\"<sigh>\",\"<chuckle>\",\"<gasp>\"]};\nconst VOICES = [\"Zephyr\",\"Puck\",\"Charon\",\"Kore\",\"Fenrir\",\"Leda\",\"Orus\",\"Aoede\",\"Callirrhoe\",\"Autonoe\",\"Enceladus\",\"Iapetus\",\"Umbriel\",\"Algieba\",\"Despina\",\"Erinome\",\"Algenib\",\"Rasalgethi\",\"Laomedeia\",\"Achernar\",\"Alnilam\",\"Schedar\",\"Gacrux\",\"Pulcherrima\",\"Achird\",\"Zubenelgenubi\",\"Vindemiatrix\",\"Sadachbia\",\"Sadaltager\",\"Sulafat\"];\nconst P = {\"langs\":{\"en\":\"English\",\"es\":\"Spanish\"},\"pace\":\"pace\",\"user\":\"Topic: {topic}\\nNotes: {notes}\",\"system\":\"You write voice-over scripts for faceless videos on the channel \\\"{channel}\\\".\\nChannel angle (every script must reflect it): {angle}\\nFormat: {format}. Niche: {niche}.\\nNarrator: {style}. Emotional arc: {arc}.\\n\\nStructure, in this order:\\n{beats}\\n\\nLength: {min}-{max} words of narration in total, aim for {goal} (it is read at about {wpm} words per minute; never fewer than {min}). Scenes: write {scenesGoal} scenes ({smin}-{smax} is fine), one idea per scene, about {perScene} words each ({sentences} sentences).\\nHook: the first sentence, short and punchy, at most {hookMax} words, no greeting and no channel name; put any context in the second sentence. Patterns that work in this niche: {hooks}. The video must pay off the hook; copy that sentence into hook_payoff.\\nWrite for the ear: short sentences, plain words, numbers written the way they are said, no symbols, no Roman numerals. {pronounce}\\nYou may add these tags, at most one every 40 words and never in the first sentence: {tags}. No other brackets, no stage directions, no speaker names, no markdown.\\nNever use these phrases: {cliches}.\\nAvoid: {avoid}. Do not invent quotes or exact statistics. If something is uncertain, say so (\\\"historians think...\\\") or leave it out. List every checkable fact in facts_to_verify.\\nVisual ideas for this niche: {visuals}.\\nWrite the script in {language}.\\n\\nReturn ONLY a JSON object:\\n{\\\"title\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"thumbnail_text\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"scenes\\\": [{\\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"shots\\\": [\\\"\\\", \\\"\\\"], \\\"on_screen\\\": \\\"\\\"}], \\\"hook_payoff\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"facts_to_verify\\\": [\\\"\\\"], \\\"pronunciations\\\": [{\\\"word\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"say\\\": \\\"\\\"}], \\\"description\\\": \\\"\\\"}\\n- \\\"text\\\": the narration of the scene. \\\"keyword\\\": the most important word of \\\"text\\\", copied exactly (it is highlighted in the captions). \\\"shots\\\": 2 stock-footage searches in English, 2-4 words each, for two different filmable shots (mix close-ups and wide shots; no text, logos or famous people). \\\"on_screen\\\": up to 5 words of on-screen text, or \\\"\\\".\\n- \\\"pronunciations\\\": only names or words a voice could misread, with a simple respelling.\\n- \\\"thumbnail_text\\\": 2-5 words. \\\"description\\\": two lines for the upload.\"};\nconst C = $('Set Channel Settings').first().json;\nconst row = $json;\nconst niche = LIB.niches[row.niche] ? row.niche : Object.keys(LIB.niches)[0];\nconst format = LIB.formats[row.format] ? row.format : 'short';\nconst N = LIB.niches[niche], F = LIB.formats[format];\nconst wpm = N.wpm || F.wpm;\nconst words = F.seconds.map(s => Math.round(s * wpm / 60));\nconst lang = ['en', 'es'].includes(row.language) ? row.language : (C.default_language || 'en');\nconst voice = VOICES.includes(String(row.voice || '').trim()) ? String(row.voice).trim() : N.voice;\nconst fill = (s, v) => s.replace(/\\{(\\w+)\\}/g, (m, k) => (k in v ? String(v[k]) : m));\nconst system = fill(P.system, { channel: C.channel_name, angle: C.channel_angle, format: F.label, niche: N.label, style: N.style, arc: N.arc,\n  beats: F.beats.map(b => '- ' + b).join('\\n'), min: words[0], max: words[1], wpm, smin: F.scenes[0], smax: F.scenes[1], hookMax: F.hookMax,\n  goal: Math.round((words[0] + words[1]) / 2), scenesGoal: Math.round((F.scenes[0] + F.scenes[1]) / 2),\n  perScene: Math.round((words[0] + words[1]) / (F.scenes[0] + F.scenes[1])), sentences: Math.max(2, Math.round((words[0] + words[1]) / (F.scenes[0] + F.scenes[1]) / 13)),\n  hooks: N.hooks.join(' | '), pronounce: N.pronounce, tags: LIB.tags.join(', '), cliches: LIB.cliches.join(', '), avoid: N.avoid, visuals: N.visuals, language: P.langs[lang] });\nconst prompt = fill(P.user, { topic: row.topic, notes: row.notes || '-' });\nreturn { json: { row_id: row.id, topic: row.topic, niche, format, lang, voice, style: N.style + '; ' + P.pace + ': ' + F.pace, words, scenes: F.scenes, hookMax: F.hookMax,\n  gender: N.gender, suno: N.suno, music: C.suno_music !== false, system, prompt } };"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"ad85d7de-d863-4857-95e8-1d9431290ed9","name":"Write Script with Gemini","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini","onError":"continueErrorOutput","maxTries":3,"position":[1600,480],"parameters":{"modelId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"id","value":"models/gemini-flash-lite-latest"},"options":{"temperature":0.9,"systemMessage":"={{ $('Build Voice Direction Prompt').item.json.system }}"},"messages":{"values":[{"content":"={{ $('Build Voice Direction Prompt').item.json.prompt }}"}]},"resource":"text","simplify":true,"operation":"message","jsonOutput":true},"retryOnFail":true,"typeVersion":1,"waitBetweenTries":3000},{"id":"736eb3ba-2f3e-448d-9088-3d111259e39b","name":"Write Script with Backup Gemini","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini","onError":"continueRegularOutput","maxTries":3,"position":[1600,710],"parameters":{"modelId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"id","value":"models/gemini-3.1-flash-lite"},"options":{"temperature":0.9,"systemMessage":"={{ $('Build Voice Direction Prompt').item.json.system }}"},"messages":{"values":[{"content":"={{ $('Build Voice Direction Prompt').item.json.prompt }}"}]},"resource":"text","simplify":true,"operation":"message","jsonOutput":true},"retryOnFail":true,"typeVersion":1,"waitBetweenTries":3000},{"id":"76924006-34e0-4731-8cce-be0b6dbe0f0d","name":"Check Script Quality","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[2160,480],"parameters":{"mode":"runOnceForEachItem","jsCode":"function readGeminiJson(s) {\r\n  let raw = s?.content?.parts?.[0]?.text ?? s?.text ?? s?.message?.content ?? (typeof s?.content === 'string' ? s.content : '') ?? '';\r\n  if (typeof raw !== 'string') raw = JSON.stringify(raw);\r\n  let a = {};\r\n  try { a = JSON.parse(raw.replace(/^```(?:json)?|```$/gm, '').trim()); } catch (e) { a = {}; }\r\n  if (Array.isArray(a)) a = a[0] ?? {};\r\n  return a && typeof a === 'object' ? a : {};\r\n}\nfunction checkScript(a, d, L) {\r\n  const words = s => (String(s).replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ').match(/[\\p{L}\\p{N}][\\p{L}\\p{N}'’-]*/gu) || []).length;\r\n  const cleaned = [];\r\n  const tagSet = new Set(L.tags);\r\n  const tidy = t => {\r\n    let s = String(t ?? '').replace(/\\*+/g, '').replace(new RegExp('^\\\\s*(' + L.speaker + ')\\\\s*:\\\\s*', 'gim'), '');\r\n    s = s.replace(/<[^>]*>/g, m => (tagSet.has(m.toLowerCase()) ? m.toLowerCase() : (cleaned.push('tag ' + m), ' ')));\r\n    s = s.replace(new RegExp('\\\\[[^\\\\]]*\\\\]|\\\\([^)]*\\\\b(' + L.direction + ')\\\\b[^)]*\\\\)', 'giu'), m => (cleaned.push('direction ' + m), ' '));\r\n    return s.replace(/[ \\t]+/g, ' ').replace(/\\s+([,.!?;:])/g, '$1').trim();\r\n  };\r\n  const scenes = (Array.isArray(a.scenes) ? a.scenes : []).map(x => (typeof x === 'string' ? { text: x } : x || {}))\r\n    .map(x => ({ text: tidy(x.text ?? x.say ?? x.narration ?? ''), keyword: String(x.keyword ?? '').trim(),\r\n      shots: [].concat(x.shots ?? x.visual ?? []).map(s => String(s).trim()).filter(Boolean).slice(0, 3), on_screen: String(x.on_screen ?? '').trim() }))\r\n    .filter(x => x.text);\r\n  // The key word must be a word of the scene (it is highlighted in the captions); if not, the longest word stands in.\r\n  for (const x of scenes) {\r\n    const plainWords = x.text.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ').match(/[\\p{L}\\p{N}][\\p{L}\\p{N}'’-]*/gu) || [];\r\n    if (!plainWords.some(w => w.toLowerCase() === x.keyword.toLowerCase())) x.keyword = [...plainWords].sort((p, q) => q.length - p.length)[0] || '';\r\n  }\r\n  if (!scenes.length) return { has_script: false, problems: [L.M.empty], cleaned };\r\n  // No tag inside the hook (first sentence) and at most one tag every 40 words.\r\n  const firstEnd = scenes[0].text.search(/[.!?](\\s|$)/);\r\n  const hookRaw = firstEnd > 0 ? scenes[0].text.slice(0, firstEnd + 1) : scenes[0].text;\r\n  if (/<[^>]+>/.test(hookRaw)) { scenes[0].text = scenes[0].text.replace(hookRaw, hookRaw.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ').replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim()); cleaned.push('tag in hook'); }\r\n  const total = scenes.reduce((n, x) => n + words(x.text), 0);\r\n  let allowed = Math.max(1, Math.floor(total / 40));\r\n  for (const x of scenes) x.text = x.text.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, m => (allowed-- > 0 ? m : (cleaned.push('extra tag'), ''))).replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\r\n  // A long hook is split at its last comma, semicolon or dash that leaves 4 to hookMax words in front: same words, a full stop\r\n  // instead of the comma (a stronger beat for the voice). Only punctuation changes.\r\n  let hook = (scenes[0].text.match(/^[^.!?]*[.!?]?/) || [''])[0].trim();\r\n  if (words(hook) > d.hookMax) {\r\n    const cuts = [...hook.matchAll(/(,|;| —| –| -)\\s+/g)].filter(m => { const n = words(hook.slice(0, m.index)); return n >= 4 && n <= d.hookMax && words(hook.slice(m.index)) >= 3; });\r\n    const cut = cuts[cuts.length - 1];\r\n    if (cut) {\r\n      const rest = hook.slice(cut.index + cut[0].length);\r\n      const fixed = hook.slice(0, cut.index) + '. ' + rest.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + rest.slice(1);\r\n      scenes[0].text = scenes[0].text.replace(hook, fixed);\r\n      cleaned.push('hook split');\r\n      hook = fixed.slice(0, cut.index + 1);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  const narration = scenes.map(x => x.text).join('\\n\\n');\r\n  const plain = narration.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ').replace(/[ \\t]+/g, ' ').replace(/ +\\n/g, '\\n').trim();\r\n  const lower = ' ' + plain.toLowerCase() + ' ';\r\n  const problems = [];\r\n  const [wMin, wMax] = d.words;\r\n  if (total < Math.round(wMin * 0.9) || total > Math.round(wMax * 1.1)) {\r\n    const goal = Math.round((wMin + wMax) / 2), dir = total < goal ? L.M.add : L.M.cut;\r\n    // Per scene, so the fix keeps the structure and adds (or trims) a sentence in each scene.\r\n    problems.push(L.M.words.replace('{n}', total).replace('{min}', wMin).replace('{max}', wMax).replace('{dir}', dir).replace('{d}', Math.abs(goal - total))\r\n      .replace('{ds}', Math.ceil(Math.abs(goal - total) / scenes.length)));\r\n  }\r\n  if (words(hook) > d.hookMax) problems.push(L.M.hook.replace('{n}', words(hook)).replace('{max}', d.hookMax));\r\n  if (scenes.length < d.scenes[0] || scenes.length > d.scenes[1]) problems.push(L.M.scenes.replace('{n}', scenes.length).replace('{min}', d.scenes[0]).replace('{max}', d.scenes[1]));\r\n  const cliches = L.cliches.filter(c => lower.includes(c.toLowerCase()));\r\n  if (cliches.length) problems.push(L.M.cliche.replace('{x}', cliches.join(', ')));\r\n  const facts = (Array.isArray(a.facts_to_verify) ? a.facts_to_verify : []).map(x => String(x).trim()).filter(Boolean);\r\n  if (!facts.length && d.niche !== 'calm') problems.push(L.M.facts);\r\n  if (scenes.some(x => !x.shots.length)) problems.push(L.M.visuals);\r\n  if (!String(a.title ?? '').trim()) problems.push(L.M.title);\r\n  if (!String(a.hook_payoff ?? '').trim()) problems.push(L.M.payoff);\r\n  const script = { title: String(a.title ?? '').trim(), thumbnail_text: String(a.thumbnail_text ?? '').trim(), scenes, hook_payoff: String(a.hook_payoff ?? '').trim(),\r\n    facts_to_verify: facts, pronunciations: (Array.isArray(a.pronunciations) ? a.pronunciations : []).filter(p => p && p.word).map(p => ({ word: String(p.word), say: String(p.say ?? '') })),\r\n    description: String(a.description ?? '').trim() };\r\n  return { has_script: true, script, narration, plain, word_count: total, hook, problems, cleaned };\r\n}\nfunction ttsBody(text, voice, style, model) {\r\n  return { model, input: [{ type: 'user_input', content: [{ type: 'text', text, annotations: [{ type: 'speech_metadata', style }] }] }],\r\n    response_format: { type: 'audio', mime_type: 'audio/wav', sample_rate: 24000 }, generation_config: { speech_config: [{ voice }] } };\r\n}\nfunction sunoBlock(c, d, S) {\r\n  const text = c.script.scenes.map(x => x.text.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ').replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim()).join('\\n\\n');\r\n  return [S.head, S.voice + ': ' + (d.gender === 'female' ? S.female : S.male) + ' · ' + S.style + ': ' + d.suno.voice + ' · ' + S.variation + ': ' + d.suno.variation,\r\n    S.music + ': ' + (d.music ? S.on + ' — ' + d.suno.music : S.off), '', S.script + ':', text].join('\\n');\r\n}\nfunction afterCheck(r, d, C, L) {\n  const base = { row_id: d.row_id, topic: d.topic, niche: d.niche, format: d.format, lang: d.lang, voice: d.voice, style: d.style, words_target: d.words };\n  if (!r.has_script) return { ...base, ...r };\n  const fix_prompt = L.fix.replace('{topic}', d.topic).replace('{script}', JSON.stringify(r.script)).replace('{problems}', r.problems.map(p => '- ' + p).join('\\n'));\n  return { ...base, ...r, fix_prompt, tts: ttsBody(r.narration, d.voice, d.style, C.tts_model || 'gemini-3.8-flash-tts'), suno_block: sunoBlock(r, d, L.S) };\n}\nconst L = {\"speaker\":\"narrator|voice ?over|vo\",\"direction\":\"pause|music|sfx|beat|sound\",\"M\":{\"empty\":\"the AI returned no script\",\"words\":\"{n} words, the format needs {min}-{max}: {dir} about {d} words, about {ds} in every scene (keep the same scenes)\",\"add\":\"add\",\"cut\":\"cut\",\"hook\":\"the hook (first sentence) has {n} words, max {max}\",\"scenes\":\"{n} scenes, the format needs {min}-{max}\",\"cliche\":\"remove these filler phrases: {x}\",\"facts\":\"list the checkable facts in facts_to_verify\",\"visuals\":\"every scene needs \\\"shots\\\": 2 stock-footage searches in English\",\"title\":\"add a title\",\"payoff\":\"add hook_payoff: the sentence that pays off the hook\"},\"fix\":\"Topic: {topic}\\n\\nYour previous script (JSON):\\n{script}\\n\\nFix ONLY these problems and return the full JSON again, same schema:\\n{problems}\\n\\nTo add words, add concrete details (names, places, causes, consequences, what it looked or sounded like), never filler. To shorten the hook, cut words or end the first sentence earlier.\",\"S\":{\"head\":\"Suno Speech · Advanced mode\",\"voice\":\"Voice\",\"female\":\"female\",\"male\":\"male\",\"style\":\"Speaking style\",\"variation\":\"Variation\",\"music\":\"Background music\",\"on\":\"on\",\"off\":\"off\",\"script\":\"Script\"},\"cliches\":[\"in this video\",\"in today's video\",\"let's dive in\",\"dive into\",\"buckle up\",\"without further ado\",\"smash that like\",\"you won't believe\",\"stay tuned\",\"hey guys\",\"welcome back\",\"let's get started\",\"mind-blowing\",\"game-changer\",\"delve\"],\"tags\":[\"<short pause>\",\"<long pause>\",\"<breath>\",\"<sigh>\",\"<chuckle>\",\"<gasp>\"]};\nconst C = $('Set Channel Settings').first().json;\nconst d = $('Build Voice Direction Prompt').item.json;\nconst r = checkScript(readGeminiJson($json), d, L);\nreturn { json: afterCheck(r, d, C, L) };"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"b8eba2fa-fc1a-44f8-b354-1eb20ceee6ba","name":"Check Script Exists","type":"n8n-nodes-base.if","position":[2480,480],"parameters":{"options":{},"conditions":{"options":{"version":2,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"loose"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"032fb120-0935-4462-9390-1ffc7809c6d4","operator":{"type":"boolean","operation":"true","singleValue":true},"leftValue":"={{ $json.has_script }}","rightValue":""}]}},"typeVersion":2.2},{"id":"d3f55d01-ba56-4737-9d6b-d614bc43f024","name":"List Topics Without Script","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[2480,1180],"parameters":{"jsCode":"const A = {\"emptyQueue\":\"🎙️ Voice Studio: your queue is empty. Add topics with the “Add topics” form and the next run will voice them.\",\"oneMissing\":\"⚠️ The AI did not write a script for “{topic}” (Gemini did not answer). It stays in the queue fo